# Keep the build context minimal and reproducible.
#
# The context is CRM_Backend/ rather than one module, because a module's pom
# declares build-tools as its parent and Maven needs that parent before it can
# read the module at all. Seven module level .dockerignore files are therefore
# replaced by this one.
#
# The Dockerfile copies build-tools/pom.xml and the module pom first so that
# dependency resolution stays cached, then the module sources. Everything below
# is noise: shipping it wastes context and risks overriding the result of the
# in-image Maven run.

# Produced inside the image. This is the entry that matters now: the context
# covers every module, so every target/ directory would otherwise be sent, and
# they are by far the largest thing in here.
*/target
target
*/bin
bin

# JVM crash artifacts
*.log
hs_err_pid*.log
replay_pid*.log

# Version control and tooling
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.mvn/wrapper/maven-wrapper.jar
.vscode
.idea
*.iml

# Local environment and credentials. Credentials must never reach an image
# layer, where they survive even if a later stage would not use them.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Runtime data written by a service
uploads/

# Editor files
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp